1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:05,322
Reviewing a long historical ECG recording
tells us what happened to a

2
00:00:05,322 --> 00:00:06,184
patient's rhythm.

3
00:00:06,184 --> 00:00:10,925
CardioTwin asks whether the earlier signal
could also support a warning

4
00:00:10,925 --> 00:00:13,942
before a new atrial fibrillation episode
begins.

5
00:00:14,062 --> 00:00:20,306
This is a research prototype, built for
the CRP Digital Twin Challenge by

6
00:00:20,306 --> 00:00:24,148
Team Lazarus from MGM's Jawaharlal Nehru
Engineering College.

7
00:00:24,148 --> 00:00:28,951
We combine historical ECG, available
patient context, saved patient state

8
00:00:28,951 --> 00:00:31,352
and a dashboard for review.

9
00:00:31,472 --> 00:00:36,856
The practical aim is to give a human
reviewer more than a number: when the

10
00:00:36,856 --> 00:00:40,804
warning was issued, which future interval
it covers, and what evidence

11
00:00:40,804 --> 00:00:41,522
supported it.

12
00:00:41,522 --> 00:00:44,393
The dashboard footage you'll see uses
manufactured data.

13
00:00:44,513 --> 00:00:48,325
We'll keep that software demonstration
separate from the real results

14
00:00:48,325 --> 00:00:49,468
throughout the video.

15
00:00:49,976 --> 00:00:52,870
Let's put the main result up front.

16
00:00:52,870 --> 00:00:57,418
The frozen finalist caught six of two
hundred and forty-one development

17
00:00:57,418 --> 00:01:01,966
events, one of forty-three primary
held-out events, and two of twenty-nine

18
00:01:01,966 --> 00:01:02,793
external events.

19
00:01:02,793 --> 00:01:06,515
That's far below our own fifty percent
sensitivity target.

20
00:01:06,515 --> 00:01:08,995
Most events had no advance warning.

21
00:01:09,115 --> 00:01:13,529
So we're presenting a working research
workflow with a negative forecasting

22
00:01:13,529 --> 00:01:13,930
result.

23
00:01:13,930 --> 00:01:16,337
The interface makes the workflow
inspectable;

24
00:01:16,337 --> 00:01:18,745
it doesn't make the predictions useful.

25
00:01:18,745 --> 00:01:23,960
We'll also look at why a low assessed
false-warning rate can be misleading

26
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:26,769
when many warnings fall outside assessable
time.

27
00:01:27,282 --> 00:01:32,797
The intended use case matters in India,
but our study contains no Indian

28
00:01:32,797 --> 00:01:34,918
recordings and no local validation.

29
00:01:34,918 --> 00:01:39,584
We can't infer Indian performance or
clinical benefit from these results.

30
00:01:39,584 --> 00:01:43,402
Public retrospective recordings let us
investigate the pipeline, check

31
00:01:43,402 --> 00:01:46,796
causal behavior and measure warnings
against saved annotations.

32
00:01:46,916 --> 00:01:51,794
They don't tell us how the system would
perform in a different population or

33
00:01:51,794 --> 00:01:52,490
care setting.

34
00:01:52,490 --> 00:01:55,974
Clinical review and prospective evaluation
would each need their own

35
00:01:55,974 --> 00:01:57,716
evidence before any deployment claim.

36
00:01:58,216 --> 00:01:59,641
Here's the fixed task.

37
00:01:59,641 --> 00:02:03,917
At each decision, the system uses the
preceding ten minutes of ECG.

38
00:02:03,917 --> 00:02:09,262
It makes a new decision every thirty
seconds and tries to warn about a new

39
00:02:09,262 --> 00:02:11,757
AF onset two to ten minutes ahead.

40
00:02:11,757 --> 00:02:14,964
We're forecasting AF onset, not heart
attack or stroke.

41
00:02:15,084 --> 00:02:19,934
In the video, manufactured dashboard
examples show how the software behaves.

42
00:02:19,934 --> 00:02:23,902
Separate saved evaluations show what
happened on real recordings.

43
00:02:23,902 --> 00:02:28,752
That separation matters whenever an
attractive demo screen appears beside a

44
00:02:28,752 --> 00:02:29,634
research result.

45
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:33,894
Follow the complete online path from left
to right.

46
00:02:33,894 --> 00:02:37,637
The replay service advances historical ECG
in thirty-second ticks.

47
00:02:37,637 --> 00:02:42,629
For each decision, it reads the preceding
ten minutes, extracts features and

48
00:02:42,629 --> 00:02:43,877
checks signal quality.

49
00:02:43,997 --> 00:02:47,460
The previous baseline is available as
patient context;

50
00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:50,922
the frozen finalist scores its own
specified inputs.

51
00:02:50,922 --> 00:02:53,952
Only after prediction does the baseline
update.

52
00:02:53,952 --> 00:02:57,848
The warning policy checks persistence,
hysteresis and cooldown before

53
00:02:57,848 --> 00:02:59,146
starting another warning.

54
00:02:59,146 --> 00:03:03,474
SQLite saves the cursor, baseline, alert
state and warning together.

55
00:03:03,594 --> 00:03:07,226
FastAPI exposes the saved state, and React
displays it.

56
00:03:07,226 --> 00:03:11,665
After a restart, replay should continue
from that cursor without repeating

57
00:03:11,665 --> 00:03:12,472
the decision.

58
00:03:12,472 --> 00:03:16,911
Each patient has separate state, so
inspecting one recording doesn't move

59
00:03:16,911 --> 00:03:18,122
another patient's clock.

60
00:03:18,641 --> 00:03:22,429
The separate offline evaluation path
checks whether warnings actually

61
00:03:22,429 --> 00:03:24,113
arrived before annotated events.

62
00:03:24,113 --> 00:03:29,164
It needs future rhythm labels to answer
that question, but those labels

63
00:03:29,164 --> 00:03:31,269
never belong in runtime inputs.

64
00:03:31,269 --> 00:03:35,478
We separate patient groups before fitting,
calibration and policy selection.

65
00:03:35,598 --> 00:03:40,326
A model package carries its configuration,
feature schema and checksums, so

66
00:03:40,326 --> 00:03:42,905
the score has an identifiable source.

67
00:03:42,905 --> 00:03:46,773
Evaluation then replays complete timelines
using the same warning

68
00:03:46,773 --> 00:03:48,492
implementation as the service.

69
00:03:48,492 --> 00:03:51,931
That connects the reported policy to
executable behavior.

70
00:03:51,931 --> 00:03:55,369
A test-access ledger records when
evaluations were used.

71
00:03:55,489 --> 00:04:00,061
It's a record of access, not proof that
every historical decision was made

72
00:04:00,061 --> 00:04:00,413
blind.

73
00:04:00,946 --> 00:04:05,089
The challenge specification asks us to
combine static patient information

74
00:04:05,089 --> 00:04:06,746
with a changing signal.

75
00:04:06,746 --> 00:04:12,132
In the real IRIDIA-AF cohort, the static
information is paired age and sex.

76
00:04:12,132 --> 00:04:16,690
We haven't filled the gaps with invented
diagnoses or laboratory results.

77
00:04:16,810 --> 00:04:21,522
The dynamic stream supplies twenty-three
causal ECG features covering heart

78
00:04:21,522 --> 00:04:24,349
rate, RR variability and recent changes.

79
00:04:24,349 --> 00:04:28,590
The frozen logistic finalist has
twenty-seven named inputs: those

80
00:04:28,590 --> 00:04:32,360
twenty-three features, age, sex and two
availability flags.

81
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:36,130
Missing values and their availability are
handled explicitly.

82
00:04:36,250 --> 00:04:41,407
The running personal baseline is saved
twin state, but it's not one of these

83
00:04:41,407 --> 00:04:42,144
predictor inputs.

84
00:04:42,144 --> 00:04:44,723
Some exploratory variants did use baseline
features;

85
00:04:44,723 --> 00:04:48,038
their inputs shouldn't be confused with
the finalist's schema.

86
00:04:48,038 --> 00:04:53,195
An ECG-only reference gives us a direct
check on whether adding age and sex

87
00:04:53,195 --> 00:04:53,564
helped.

88
00:04:54,098 --> 00:04:57,967
That's what digital twin means in this
project: saved patient-specific

89
00:04:57,967 --> 00:05:01,061
history and a replay a reviewer can
inspect.

90
00:05:01,061 --> 00:05:04,930
We aren't simulating an anatomical heart
or continually retraining the

91
00:05:04,930 --> 00:05:05,317
model.

92
00:05:05,317 --> 00:05:09,959
The code can accept more clinical fields
than our real cohort provides.

93
00:05:10,079 --> 00:05:14,656
Manufactured profiles let us exercise
those interface fields, but they don't

94
00:05:14,656 --> 00:05:17,153
establish richer fusion on real patients.

95
00:05:17,153 --> 00:05:21,731
In the actual comparison, adding the
available patient context showed no

96
00:05:21,731 --> 00:05:22,563
fusion benefit.

97
00:05:22,563 --> 00:05:26,724
We report that outcome alongside the
software capability, because connecting

98
00:05:26,724 --> 00:05:29,637
two streams alone doesn't demonstrate
better forecasting.

99
00:05:30,150 --> 00:05:32,743
We're now moving into the dashboard.

100
00:05:32,743 --> 00:05:38,362
Both the ECG and clinical profiles in this
footage are manufactured, and its

101
00:05:38,362 --> 00:05:40,955
model was trained on synthetic examples.

102
00:05:40,955 --> 00:05:43,980
This shows software behavior, not patient
performance.

103
00:05:43,980 --> 00:05:49,166
The normal server refuses to serve the
real finalist because it failed

104
00:05:49,166 --> 00:05:50,031
acceptance gates.

105
00:05:50,151 --> 00:05:55,347
There's an explicit research mode with a
red warning banner, but this video

106
00:05:55,347 --> 00:05:57,346
doesn't replay a real record.

107
00:05:57,346 --> 00:06:01,743
We'll show the real-data findings
separately from saved reports after the

108
00:06:01,743 --> 00:06:02,143
demonstration.

109
00:06:02,660 --> 00:06:05,898
Start with the patient selector and the
clock.

110
00:06:05,898 --> 00:06:08,326
This clock belongs to the recording;

111
00:06:08,326 --> 00:06:10,754
it isn't the current wall time.

112
00:06:10,754 --> 00:06:16,014
The ECG panel shows the most recent ten
seconds, while the predictor uses

113
00:06:16,014 --> 00:06:17,633
the preceding ten minutes.

114
00:06:17,633 --> 00:06:20,466
Heart-rate and RR trends summarize earlier
decisions.

115
00:06:20,586 --> 00:06:23,163
The patient-context values here are
manufactured;

116
00:06:23,163 --> 00:06:26,598
real IRIDIA data provide age and sex only.

117
00:06:26,598 --> 00:06:31,323
We also downsample the displayed ECG so
the trace stays readable.

118
00:06:31,323 --> 00:06:36,477
That display isn't the exact array used
for feature extraction, and fewer

119
00:06:36,477 --> 00:06:39,912
points on screen don't shorten the
prediction window.

120
00:06:40,032 --> 00:06:44,225
Source sampling rate, signal quality and
forecast availability are visible

121
00:06:44,225 --> 00:06:45,483
beside the result.

122
00:06:45,483 --> 00:06:50,515
Together, they help a reviewer check what
the displayed score rests on

123
00:06:50,515 --> 00:06:51,773
before interpreting it.

124
00:06:52,290 --> 00:06:54,579
Replay runs faster than real time.

125
00:06:54,579 --> 00:06:58,775
At the default setting, each wall second
advances thirty seconds of

126
00:06:58,775 --> 00:06:59,538
historical recording.

127
00:06:59,538 --> 00:07:04,878
This is a simulation of saved data, not a
wearable connection or a live

128
00:07:04,878 --> 00:07:05,641
hospital feed.

129
00:07:05,761 --> 00:07:09,745
Early decisions can remain unavailable
while the system collects enough

130
00:07:09,745 --> 00:07:12,135
history and prior reliable baseline
updates.

131
00:07:12,135 --> 00:07:14,525
That warm-up has an explicit reason.

132
00:07:14,525 --> 00:07:16,517
It isn't a zero-risk estimate.

133
00:07:16,517 --> 00:07:20,899
Watch the recording clock and the
availability message together as replay

134
00:07:20,899 --> 00:07:21,298
progresses.

135
00:07:21,805 --> 00:07:23,698
Pause holds the replay position.

136
00:07:23,698 --> 00:07:28,243
Step moves forward by one decision, so
changes are easier to inspect.

137
00:07:28,243 --> 00:07:33,166
The forecast panel records an issue time,
its future target interval and the

138
00:07:33,166 --> 00:07:34,302
frozen model version.

139
00:07:34,302 --> 00:07:38,467
The percentage is a calibrated model
score, not a clinically validated

140
00:07:38,467 --> 00:07:38,846
probability.

141
00:07:38,966 --> 00:07:42,010
Passing the quality check is only one
requirement.

142
00:07:42,010 --> 00:07:46,575
The system also needs enough history,
completed warm-up and a loaded model

143
00:07:46,575 --> 00:07:50,760
compatible with the runtime configuration
before it can provide a forecast.

144
00:07:51,283 --> 00:07:55,201
The baseline summarizes earlier reliable
feature values and updates after

145
00:07:55,201 --> 00:07:55,593
prediction.

146
00:07:55,593 --> 00:08:00,294
When it moves, that doesn't mean the model
has learned new weights.

147
00:08:00,294 --> 00:08:04,996
For the real finalist, it's contextual
patient state rather than a predictor

148
00:08:04,996 --> 00:08:05,387
input.

149
00:08:05,507 --> 00:08:10,043
The evidence table shows large
contributions to the raw model score and

150
00:08:10,043 --> 00:08:12,689
compares available values with earlier
baseline context.

151
00:08:12,689 --> 00:08:16,092
This helps explain how the model reached
its score.

152
00:08:16,092 --> 00:08:21,006
It doesn't identify causes of AF or
recommend a treatment for the patient.

153
00:08:21,517 --> 00:08:25,437
A warning needs persistently elevated
scores under the configured policy.

154
00:08:25,437 --> 00:08:29,749
Its saved record includes the issue time,
future interval, model identity

155
00:08:29,749 --> 00:08:30,925
and feature evidence.

156
00:08:30,925 --> 00:08:36,021
The reviewer can mark it reviewed,
dismissed or pending, and add a note.

157
00:08:36,021 --> 00:08:39,157
Those actions stay in history, making
review traceable.

158
00:08:39,277 --> 00:08:42,909
They don't change whether the warning
predicted an event correctly.

159
00:08:42,909 --> 00:08:46,541
A dismissed false warning remains a false
warning in evaluation.

160
00:08:46,541 --> 00:08:49,811
The software doesn't make a diagnosis or
choose treatment.

161
00:08:50,336 --> 00:08:55,136
Patient zero has an intentionally
unreliable stretch in this manufactured

162
00:08:55,136 --> 00:08:55,616
ECG.

163
00:08:55,616 --> 00:08:59,935
Look at the quality reason beside the
unavailable forecast.

164
00:08:59,935 --> 00:09:03,295
The system declines to score this
decision;

165
00:09:03,295 --> 00:09:06,654
it isn't saying the patient is safe.

166
00:09:06,654 --> 00:09:10,014
In real evaluation, rejected time stays
visible.

167
00:09:10,134 --> 00:09:14,131
An event missed during abstention still
counts as missed.

168
00:09:14,131 --> 00:09:18,129
Refusing difficult periods must not make
missed events disappear.

169
00:09:18,656 --> 00:09:20,915
Sometimes the warning list is quiet.

170
00:09:20,915 --> 00:09:25,057
The interface preserves that state without
creating an alert, but silence

171
00:09:25,057 --> 00:09:27,316
doesn't mean the patient is safe.

172
00:09:27,316 --> 00:09:29,576
Pause only stops replay from progressing.

173
00:09:29,576 --> 00:09:33,718
Reset goes further: it restarts this
patient's replay and clears their

174
00:09:33,718 --> 00:09:35,224
warning and review history.

175
00:09:35,344 --> 00:09:37,586
Those controls have different purposes.

176
00:09:37,586 --> 00:09:42,517
Saved state helps review, while this
manufactured example tells us nothing

177
00:09:42,517 --> 00:09:43,861
about clinical reliability.

178
00:09:44,383 --> 00:09:47,399
This screen also uses made-up data.

179
00:09:47,399 --> 00:09:51,924
It shows metrics, calibration plots,
misses and warning outcomes.

180
00:09:51,924 --> 00:09:54,940
These aren't the project's real results.

181
00:09:54,940 --> 00:09:57,956
They're examples that test the screen.

182
00:09:57,956 --> 00:10:03,989
Next, we'll leave the demo and look at the
weak frozen results.

183
00:10:04,502 --> 00:10:09,966
A saved real development-record prefix has
seventy-two replay steps: median

184
00:10:09,966 --> 00:10:13,244
twenty-five milliseconds, ninety-fifth
percentile twenty-seven milliseconds

185
00:10:13,244 --> 00:10:14,337
per step.

186
00:10:14,337 --> 00:10:19,801
Changing only future signal or labels left
earlier outputs unchanged.

187
00:10:19,801 --> 00:10:25,266
These checks support causal behavior and
show local run cost.

188
00:10:25,266 --> 00:10:29,637
They don't prove useful forecasting or
wearable speed.

189
00:10:30,150 --> 00:10:32,593
First, we keep people apart.

190
00:10:32,593 --> 00:10:37,968
Overlapping windows from one person's ECG
share a lot of information.

191
00:10:37,968 --> 00:10:43,832
Randomly mixing them between training and
testing could make the task look

192
00:10:43,832 --> 00:10:44,320
easier.

193
00:10:44,320 --> 00:10:50,184
We split patient groups and keep whole
timelines, including records with no

194
00:10:50,184 --> 00:10:51,161
eligible events.

195
00:10:51,281 --> 00:10:54,435
That measures warnings across monitoring
time.

196
00:10:54,435 --> 00:10:59,166
Correct software and useful advance
warning are separate tests.

197
00:10:59,680 --> 00:11:03,908
Where needed, fitting, early stopping,
calibration and warning-policy choice

198
00:11:03,908 --> 00:11:05,318
use separate roles.

199
00:11:05,318 --> 00:11:10,485
We froze weights, calibration and policy
before primary and external tests.

200
00:11:10,485 --> 00:11:16,593
We've now seen those cohorts, so a new
tuning cycle can't call them

201
00:11:16,593 --> 00:11:17,063
untouched.

202
00:11:17,063 --> 00:11:21,291
Fresh output folders and source-bound
receipts preserve each run.

203
00:11:21,411 --> 00:11:25,778
Future model choice needs development
evidence, then a fresh cohort to

204
00:11:25,778 --> 00:11:26,572
confirm it.

205
00:11:26,572 --> 00:11:29,749
An already seen test set can't do that.

206
00:11:30,259 --> 00:11:33,127
We test whole records, not selected
windows.

207
00:11:33,127 --> 00:11:38,865
A warning can match at most one eligible
event, two to ten minutes ahead,

208
00:11:38,865 --> 00:11:40,094
including both ends.

209
00:11:40,094 --> 00:11:42,553
An event can be matched once.

210
00:11:42,553 --> 00:11:47,880
If all chances to warn were unavailable,
the event still counts as missed.

211
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:52,891
Warnings during AF, post-AF washout or
unknown-outcome time are counted

212
00:11:52,891 --> 00:11:53,380
separately.

213
00:11:53,380 --> 00:11:57,782
Those parts of the timeline stay in the
report.

214
00:11:58,306 --> 00:12:00,562
The denominator matters too.

215
00:12:00,562 --> 00:12:05,638
We divide assessed false warnings by
labelled, forecast-eligible hours,

216
00:12:05,638 --> 00:12:07,893
including quality-rejected eligible
windows.

217
00:12:07,893 --> 00:12:15,225
Using all recorded hours would let unknown
or excluded time dilute the rate.

218
00:12:15,225 --> 00:12:16,917
Coverage is separate.

219
00:12:17,037 --> 00:12:22,317
Events need enough labelled non-AF
history, an episode of at least thirty

220
00:12:22,317 --> 00:12:25,396
seconds, the target interval and post-AF
washout.

221
00:12:25,396 --> 00:12:31,116
We report counts with rates, so readers
can see which hours and warnings

222
00:12:31,116 --> 00:12:31,996
were assessed.

223
00:12:32,519 --> 00:12:37,777
IRIDIA-AF has one hundred and sixty-seven
recordings from one hundred and

224
00:12:37,777 --> 00:12:42,557
fifty-two patients: about six thousand six
hundred and ninety hours.

225
00:12:42,557 --> 00:12:47,815
Development has one hundred and twenty-one
patient groups and two hundred

226
00:12:47,815 --> 00:12:49,727
and forty-one eligible events.

227
00:12:49,727 --> 00:12:54,507
The frozen primary cohort has thirty-one
groups and forty-three events.

228
00:12:54,627 --> 00:12:59,027
LTAF adds twenty-nine events across
eighty-four recording groups.

229
00:12:59,027 --> 00:13:05,078
We haven't verified patient identity
across its records, so those groups

230
00:13:05,078 --> 00:13:08,378
can't simply be called independent people.

231
00:13:08,896 --> 00:13:14,634
Our limits are at most zero point two five
assessed false warnings per

232
00:13:14,634 --> 00:13:18,607
eligible hour and at least fifty percent
event sensitivity.

233
00:13:18,607 --> 00:13:23,021
These are research assumptions, not
clinical standards or an organizer's

234
00:13:23,021 --> 00:13:23,903
required accuracy.

235
00:13:23,903 --> 00:13:25,228
Both must pass.

236
00:13:25,228 --> 00:13:29,642
Few false warnings can't make up for
missing most events.

237
00:13:30,150 --> 00:13:32,104
The synthetic demonstration has ended.

238
00:13:32,104 --> 00:13:36,012
These are the frozen finalist's saved
results on real recordings.

239
00:13:36,500 --> 00:13:41,055
Development caught six of two hundred and
forty-one events.

240
00:13:41,055 --> 00:13:45,103
The primary held-out cohort caught one of
forty-three.

241
00:13:45,103 --> 00:13:47,634
LTAF caught two of twenty-nine.

242
00:13:47,634 --> 00:13:53,201
That's about two to seven percent
sensitivity, well below fifty percent.

243
00:13:53,201 --> 00:13:57,249
Acceptance fails despite assessed
false-warning rates below budget.

244
00:13:57,249 --> 00:14:00,286
Most events had no advance warning.

245
00:14:00,799 --> 00:14:04,729
Primary AUROC was zero point six one one;

246
00:14:04,729 --> 00:14:08,659
LTAF AUROC was zero point six three one.

247
00:14:08,659 --> 00:14:14,063
This measures score ranking across
thresholds, not events caught by the

248
00:14:14,063 --> 00:14:17,010
chosen policy within its false-warning
budget.

249
00:14:17,010 --> 00:14:20,940
The few events caught remain the main
result.

250
00:14:21,453 --> 00:14:26,780
We compared saved score timing with random
shifts within each record,

251
00:14:26,780 --> 00:14:27,748
without refitting.

252
00:14:27,748 --> 00:14:33,075
Development caught six events, versus
about four point five expected at

253
00:14:33,075 --> 00:14:33,559
random.

254
00:14:33,559 --> 00:14:38,886
The held-out cohorts together caught three
of seventy-two, versus about zero

255
00:14:38,886 --> 00:14:40,339
point seven expected.

256
00:14:40,339 --> 00:14:42,760
Three events are little evidence.

257
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:47,307
The intervals include zero, and this was a
post-hoc check.

258
00:14:47,307 --> 00:14:50,848
We claim no demonstrated event-level skill
from it.

259
00:14:51,366 --> 00:14:55,052
LTAF had three hundred and ninety-eight
warning starts.

260
00:14:55,052 --> 00:14:59,659
Three hundred and ninety-two couldn't be
assessed: two hundred and

261
00:14:59,659 --> 00:15:04,267
twenty-two during AF, seventy-seven in
washout and ninety-three in unknown

262
00:15:04,267 --> 00:15:04,727
time.

263
00:15:04,727 --> 00:15:07,492
Only four were assessed false warnings.

264
00:15:07,612 --> 00:15:12,446
The zero point zero zero eight assessed
rate needs that full inventory

265
00:15:12,446 --> 00:15:13,251
beside it.

266
00:15:13,251 --> 00:15:18,085
Randomly placing the same warning time
gives about zero point one zero

267
00:15:18,085 --> 00:15:20,099
assessed false warnings per hour.

268
00:15:20,099 --> 00:15:23,322
A low assessed rate alone doesn't show
skill.

269
00:15:23,843 --> 00:15:25,185
Fusion didn't help.

270
00:15:25,185 --> 00:15:31,003
ECG alone caught seven development events,
versus six for age, sex and ECG.

271
00:15:31,003 --> 00:15:36,373
The finalist's development Brier score was
zero point zero zero eight three

272
00:15:36,373 --> 00:15:37,268
eight four.

273
00:15:37,268 --> 00:15:42,191
The observed constant base-rate reference
scored zero point zero zero eight

274
00:15:42,191 --> 00:15:43,534
three five eight.

275
00:15:43,654 --> 00:15:47,415
Lower is better, but the simple reference
did as well.

276
00:15:47,415 --> 00:15:50,049
The small error doesn't show forecasting
value.

277
00:15:50,563 --> 00:15:54,984
Other tests used gradient boosting,
personal-baseline features, ectopy-like

278
00:15:54,984 --> 00:15:57,748
motifs and RR temporal CNNs.

279
00:15:57,748 --> 00:16:02,723
The RR models caught four and seven
development events.

280
00:16:02,723 --> 00:16:08,250
A waveform CNN caught four, with about
thirty-three percent warning-state

281
00:16:08,250 --> 00:16:08,803
occupancy.

282
00:16:08,803 --> 00:16:11,014
Precursor ranking caught five.

283
00:16:11,014 --> 00:16:13,777
ECGFounder had zero outcome fits.

284
00:16:13,897 --> 00:16:18,800
Its last cloud job failed in dependency
setup, before data reads.

285
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:22,366
Progress on an encoder doesn't show better
forecasting.

286
00:16:22,888 --> 00:16:27,417
A development-fold calibration defect
reversed ranking from zero point five

287
00:16:27,417 --> 00:16:31,040
seven three to zero point four two seven.

288
00:16:31,040 --> 00:16:35,116
The frozen finalists have positive slopes
and are unaffected.

289
00:16:35,116 --> 00:16:38,286
A later exploratory guard rejects
non-positive slopes.

290
00:16:38,286 --> 00:16:42,362
It doesn't repair history or change these
saved results.

291
00:16:42,866 --> 00:16:46,299
Published comparisons use different
reporting and omit the operating

292
00:16:46,299 --> 00:16:48,206
false-alarm evidence we need here.

293
00:16:48,206 --> 00:16:53,164
We keep them as context rather than proof
that our target is achievable.

294
00:16:53,164 --> 00:16:57,741
Closed attempts retain their failures and
limitations, so a later reader can

295
00:16:57,741 --> 00:16:59,648
see what was actually tested.

296
00:17:00,150 --> 00:17:03,231
The limits go beyond missed events.

297
00:17:03,231 --> 00:17:08,366
These are retrospective public records,
not a prospective device study.

298
00:17:08,366 --> 00:17:13,501
We have no Indian-population evidence,
secured clinical partner or treatment

299
00:17:13,501 --> 00:17:14,015
advice.

300
00:17:14,015 --> 00:17:17,609
Patient identity across LTAF records is
unverified.

301
00:17:17,609 --> 00:17:21,204
Development results follow tests of many
candidates.

302
00:17:21,324 --> 00:17:25,738
Already seen test cohorts can't provide
fresh confirmation.

303
00:17:25,738 --> 00:17:31,255
Clinical data are limited, and signal
preprocessing varies by source.

304
00:17:31,255 --> 00:17:35,118
RR variability isn't automatically
validated normal-to-normal heart-rate

305
00:17:35,118 --> 00:17:35,669
variability.

306
00:17:35,669 --> 00:17:41,739
Local replay speed describes this software
and workload, not battery use,

307
00:17:41,739 --> 00:17:45,049
wireless reliability or continuous
wearable performance.

308
00:17:45,169 --> 00:17:49,429
The dashboard's made-up profiles must stay
separate from real patient

309
00:17:49,429 --> 00:17:49,855
evidence.

310
00:17:49,855 --> 00:17:54,967
These limits define what the prototype
shows and what still needs another

311
00:17:54,967 --> 00:17:55,393
study.

312
00:17:55,918 --> 00:18:00,716
A future validation program would start
with an ethically approved clinical

313
00:18:00,716 --> 00:18:03,768
partner and a clearly specified monitoring
setting.

314
00:18:03,768 --> 00:18:08,130
Before fitting another model, we'd declare
the target, patient roles,

315
00:18:08,130 --> 00:18:11,182
missing-data rules, warning budget and
advancement gates.

316
00:18:11,182 --> 00:18:13,799
Measurement and calibration need diagnosis
first.

317
00:18:13,919 --> 00:18:18,641
Then we'd compare a candidate with simple
references on the same complete

318
00:18:18,641 --> 00:18:22,183
timelines, so every method faces the same
warning task.

319
00:18:22,183 --> 00:18:26,119
Failed attempts would remain saved, with
thresholds unchanged after seeing

320
00:18:26,119 --> 00:18:26,906
their results.

321
00:18:27,026 --> 00:18:32,442
If a model earned further study, the next
step would be a fresh prospective

322
00:18:32,442 --> 00:18:36,310
silent evaluation: log alerts without
showing them to clinicians, then

323
00:18:36,310 --> 00:18:39,792
assess events, false warnings, coverage
and burden, including uncertainty.

324
00:18:39,792 --> 00:18:44,435
A separate later study could ask whether
acting on warnings improves care.

325
00:18:44,555 --> 00:18:46,707
We haven't completed those stages.

326
00:18:46,707 --> 00:18:51,872
For this submission, we preserve the weak
forecasting result and make the

327
00:18:51,872 --> 00:18:55,745
workflow inspectable, reproducible and
clear about what remains unmeasured.

328
00:18:55,745 --> 00:18:59,619
The acceptance gates remain research
assumptions throughout that process.

329
00:19:00,150 --> 00:19:06,548
The public GitHub repository is Lazarus,
MGM, Jawaharlal Nehru Engineering

330
00:19:06,548 --> 00:19:08,467
College, under sumitjadhav1703.

331
00:19:08,467 --> 00:19:14,225
It includes source, locked dependencies,
tests, selected reports and

332
00:19:14,225 --> 00:19:15,504
submission documents.

333
00:19:15,504 --> 00:19:22,541
Raw ECG, model binaries, local patient
state and private receipts are

334
00:19:22,541 --> 00:19:23,181
omitted.

335
00:19:23,301 --> 00:19:28,314
The recorded seventeenth October public
run had eight hundred and forty-one

336
00:19:28,314 --> 00:19:31,049
passes and eighty-three skips without
PyTorch.

337
00:19:31,049 --> 00:19:35,150
That's a historical run, not a fresh test
claim.

338
00:19:35,150 --> 00:19:38,340
The full repository address stays on
screen.

339
00:19:38,340 --> 00:19:40,619
Data retain their own licences;

340
00:19:40,619 --> 00:19:42,442
code is MIT licensed.

341
00:19:42,965 --> 00:19:45,102
CardioTwin is a research prototype.

342
00:19:45,102 --> 00:19:47,667
This video's dashboard footage is
synthetic.

343
00:19:47,667 --> 00:19:52,370
Its contribution is causal replay, clear
evaluation gates and a documented

344
00:19:52,370 --> 00:19:53,653
negative forecasting result.

345
00:19:53,653 --> 00:19:57,500
A usable interface hasn't made the model
clinically useful.

346
00:19:57,500 --> 00:19:59,638
Thank you from Team Lazarus.
